1
00:01:52,363 --> 00:01:53,964
What's wrong, little lady?

2
00:01:54,165 --> 00:01:55,900
I'm hungry...

3
00:01:56,400 --> 00:01:58,702
You haven't had lunch yet?

4
00:01:58,903 --> 00:01:59,537
No.

5
00:01:59,737 --> 00:02:00,871
Where's your mom?

6
00:02:16,220 --> 00:02:18,889
Not now. I'm busy.

7
00:02:19,456 --> 00:02:22,059
I said, "Not now!"

8
00:02:23,461 --> 00:02:24,728
What are you doing?

9
00:02:25,296 --> 00:02:29,600
You call yourself a mother when you don't even feed your kid?

10
00:02:29,834 --> 00:02:31,135
Hey, butt out, lady.

11
00:02:32,102 --> 00:02:34,071
What gives you the right, huh?

12
00:02:35,139 --> 00:02:36,907
It's none of your business.

13
00:02:41,712 --> 00:02:42,746
Exchange these.

14
00:02:44,782 --> 00:02:46,250
I'm really sorry!

15
00:02:46,450 --> 00:02:49,954
Never again will I neglect my daughter to play pachinko.

16
00:02:50,321 --> 00:02:52,456
Mariko, let's go eat.

17
00:02:52,690 --> 00:02:53,457
Okay.

18
00:02:55,159 --> 00:02:56,227
Thank you!

19
00:03:02,766 --> 00:03:03,567
Huh?

20
00:03:06,170 --> 00:03:08,806
What the heck? This sucks.

21
00:03:09,039 --> 00:03:10,641
What's wrong, Naoko-chan?

22
00:03:10,875 --> 00:03:13,711
Oh, Reiko! Get a load of this.

23
00:03:13,911 --> 00:03:16,313
We just gave this guy a parking ticket,

24
00:03:16,514 --> 00:03:19,717
but now he's hitting on Komachi!

25
00:03:19,917 --> 00:03:23,187
No, I couldn't accept such flowers...

26
00:03:23,587 --> 00:03:27,491
You're the type of gal who belongs in the passenger seat of my Porsche.

27
00:03:27,725 --> 00:03:31,462
Even this bouquet of roses pales in comparison to your beauty.

28
00:03:31,829 --> 00:03:33,531
D-Do you think so?

29
00:03:33,764 --> 00:03:37,334
How about it? Want to go for a drive to Yokohama?

30
00:03:37,735 --> 00:03:40,905
We can dine at a fancy restaurant as we watch the sun set.

31
00:03:41,105 --> 00:03:43,941
But I'm still on duty...

32
00:03:44,141 --> 00:03:47,311
That's rare, a pearl white Porsche.

33
00:03:47,511 --> 00:03:48,312
Hmm?

34
00:04:01,825 --> 00:04:04,028
ELITE

35
00:04:05,863 --> 00:04:09,333
But if you insist, I suppose I could leave early...

36
00:04:09,533 --> 00:04:10,167
Huh?

37
00:04:10,935 --> 00:04:15,839
A female that knows there's only one pearl white Porsche in Japan?

38
00:04:16,040 --> 00:04:18,709
It's a pleasure to meet you, mad... madmos...

39
00:04:18,943 --> 00:04:20,711
Do you mean "mademoiselle"?

40
00:04:20,945 --> 00:04:25,049
That's the one. You are my ideal mad... madmos...

41
00:04:25,249 --> 00:04:26,383
Mademoiselle.

42
00:04:26,984 --> 00:04:30,888
In other words, the passenger seat of my car was made just for you.

43
00:04:31,555 --> 00:04:34,158
Want to go for a drive to Yokohama?

44
00:04:34,992 --> 00:04:38,696
Sorry, but I prefer to sit in the driver's seat.

45
00:04:38,896 --> 00:04:42,499
Plus, you shouldn't use words that are too big for you.

46
00:04:44,234 --> 00:04:49,340
My lady, I forgot to mention. I'm Reiji Shiratori, and I'm super loaded.

47
00:04:49,540 --> 00:04:52,276
Oh? Which university did I go to?

48
00:04:52,910 --> 00:04:54,078
Hmm...

49
00:04:55,045 --> 00:04:56,880
Oukei University, of course.

50
00:04:57,348 --> 00:04:59,049
Nobody asked.

51
00:04:59,249 --> 00:05:00,384
Let's go.

52
00:05:02,686 --> 00:05:04,922
What's that? Where do I live?

53
00:05:05,155 --> 00:05:08,625
Why, Den-en-chofu, of course. It's a 150 tsubo plot of land.

54
00:05:08,859 --> 00:05:10,828
What's that? You're impressed?

55
00:05:11,028 --> 00:05:12,529
Oh, it's nothing special.

56
00:05:12,730 --> 00:05:15,833
-Keep bragging, 'cause no one's listening. -Huh?

57
00:05:16,033 --> 00:05:18,936
You better pay the fine, you loser!

58
00:05:20,037 --> 00:05:23,207
Hmph, I don't take advice from trollops.

59
00:05:25,376 --> 00:05:27,945
My lady, I have a Porsche.

60
00:05:28,178 --> 00:05:30,280
You cannot escape me!

61
00:05:40,090 --> 00:05:41,859
He's chasing us.

62
00:05:42,059 --> 00:05:44,061
We'll never outrun a Porsche.

63
00:05:48,332 --> 00:05:51,135
Don't worry. He'll never catch us driving like that.

64
00:05:55,205 --> 00:05:56,874
Damn it! Stupid car!

65
00:05:57,341 --> 00:05:59,743
Can't handle my super-quick gear changes?

66
00:05:59,943 --> 00:06:01,078
Piece of junk!

67
00:06:03,747 --> 00:06:07,885
Hmm, I knew women were getting addicted to the slots,

68
00:06:08,085 --> 00:06:10,521
but I didn't think it extended to mothers.

69
00:06:10,954 --> 00:06:13,590
Certainly a dysfunction within societal order.

70
00:06:13,791 --> 00:06:14,692
Huh?

71
00:06:15,159 --> 00:06:17,327
What? What'd I say?

72
00:06:17,828 --> 00:06:21,799
We're just surprised to hear you say the phrase "societal order."

73
00:06:22,332 --> 00:06:25,903
Ryotsu. How good of you to have a mind for societal issues.

74
00:06:26,970 --> 00:06:28,272
You think so?

75
00:06:28,472 --> 00:06:33,444
Well, it's been harder to nab a seat that pays out with more women around.

76
00:06:33,644 --> 00:06:35,979
We simply must do something about this.

77
00:06:36,480 --> 00:06:38,015
You moron!

78
00:06:38,248 --> 00:06:40,350
You are an absolute dreg of society!

79
00:06:40,684 --> 00:06:42,019
C-Chief!

80
00:06:42,920 --> 00:06:43,954
What's that noise?

81
00:06:46,123 --> 00:06:47,257
Oh no...

82
00:06:47,791 --> 00:06:49,193
This is bad.

83
00:06:49,393 --> 00:06:51,295
Reiko-san, what's wrong?

84
00:06:51,495 --> 00:06:54,998
The pretentious guy in that Porsche keeps trying to hit on me.

85
00:06:58,102 --> 00:07:00,170
He stalled it.

86
00:07:00,370 --> 00:07:02,139
That Porsche must be crying.

87
00:07:02,506 --> 00:07:04,975
Blast! Why did you stop?

88
00:07:07,010 --> 00:07:09,313
Damn it! Stupid hunk of junk!

89
00:07:17,020 --> 00:07:19,890
What a terrible driver. Who is this guy?

90
00:07:25,028 --> 00:07:27,664
Behold! A diamond-encrusted Rolax on my left hand!

91
00:07:28,532 --> 00:07:30,667
An Armoni jacket and coat!

92
00:07:31,401 --> 00:07:33,170
A Fentix tie!

93
00:07:33,971 --> 00:07:35,172
Herragamo shoes!

94
00:07:36,907 --> 00:07:38,842
This outfit cost ten million yen.

95
00:07:39,209 --> 00:07:43,213
My name is Reiji Shiratori, and I'm super loaded!

96
00:07:44,248 --> 00:07:46,917
Is that like being a Super Saiyan?

97
00:07:48,018 --> 00:07:49,319
No!

98
00:07:50,320 --> 00:07:51,922
Oh, he's just an idiot.

99
00:07:52,156 --> 00:07:53,223
Let's go inside.

100
00:07:53,423 --> 00:07:54,224
Hey!

101
00:07:56,326 --> 00:08:00,464
You've got guts to ignore me. I'll give you credit for that.

102
00:08:00,697 --> 00:08:02,566
Don't follow us in!

103
00:08:02,766 --> 00:08:04,434
I'm not here for you.

104
00:08:04,635 --> 00:08:07,337
Be gone. I'm here for someone else.

105
00:08:08,105 --> 00:08:13,443
You are cruel, fair maiden, to make Reiji Shiratori fall for you on sight.

106
00:08:14,411 --> 00:08:16,647
I'm busy today. I'll see you around.

107
00:08:17,814 --> 00:08:18,749
Tut, tut.

108
00:08:18,949 --> 00:08:22,052
Not on my watch. I'll not let you through my grasp again.

109
00:08:22,252 --> 00:08:25,556
For you are the lucky one who gets to ride in my Porsche.

110
00:08:26,423 --> 00:08:29,226
Nobody wants to ride in a stalling Porsche.

111
00:08:29,927 --> 00:08:32,029
I stopped there on purpose!

112
00:08:32,229 --> 00:08:34,231
I didn't stall!

113
00:08:34,431 --> 00:08:37,234
All right! Don't get your panties in a knot.

114
00:08:37,601 --> 00:08:41,738
Come, my lady. Let us go for a drive in my Porsche.

115
00:08:41,939 --> 00:08:43,407
I'm on duty, so no.

116
00:08:44,141 --> 00:08:46,677
Then how about dinner after work?

117
00:08:46,910 --> 00:08:49,213
I know a place in Ginza.

118
00:08:50,214 --> 00:08:51,748
I have plans tonight.

119
00:08:51,949 --> 00:08:54,451
What's that? Where's my house?

120
00:08:55,519 --> 00:08:58,956
Den-en-chofu, right? You said so earlier.

121
00:08:59,156 --> 00:09:00,824
Y-Yes, I did.

122
00:09:01,058 --> 00:09:02,693
What's that? My parentage?

123
00:09:03,493 --> 00:09:05,162
He's talking to himself.

124
00:09:05,395 --> 00:09:07,297
My Dad owns Shiratori Ironworks.

125
00:09:07,497 --> 00:09:10,667
I'm next in line to be president. Impressive, no?

126
00:09:12,135 --> 00:09:14,304
I said no more running away, sweetheart.

127
00:09:16,406 --> 00:09:19,776
Shiratori Ironworks is a highly respected company, isn't it?

128
00:09:19,977 --> 00:09:22,479
I've seen their commercials on TV.

129
00:09:22,679 --> 00:09:25,649
Oh, the one with the father and son talking by the sea?

130
00:09:25,849 --> 00:09:27,818
You plebs know it?

131
00:09:31,455 --> 00:09:33,957
You are rigid and inflexible, Dad.

132
00:09:34,157 --> 00:09:37,427
Well, I do work with iron after all.

133
00:09:37,628 --> 00:09:40,197
You've sure got me there.

134
00:09:46,103 --> 00:09:48,639
Shiratori Ironworks. For a better tomorrow.

135
00:09:49,172 --> 00:09:51,742
That's my dad in the commercial.

136
00:09:51,975 --> 00:09:53,343
Well? Impressive, no?

137
00:09:53,543 --> 00:09:55,812
It's impressively cringeworthy.

138
00:09:56,013 --> 00:09:57,314
Shut up!

139
00:09:57,514 --> 00:10:02,052
All you people do is grumble and complain. That's why I can't stand the poor!

140
00:10:02,286 --> 00:10:07,057
Reiko-san, just keep moving to his right to get away from him.

141
00:10:08,225 --> 00:10:12,329
You don't even know the hardships of inheritance tax! You're just jealous...

142
00:10:12,529 --> 00:10:13,330
Hmm?

143
00:10:13,530 --> 00:10:15,732
My lady, how many times must I tell you...

144
00:10:21,672 --> 00:10:23,173
My lady... Um, me and you...

145
00:10:23,373 --> 00:10:24,174
What the...?

146
00:10:24,374 --> 00:10:28,178
Damn it! Stop mocking me!

147
00:10:34,584 --> 00:10:37,521
I'll never give up, my lady!

148
00:10:37,955 --> 00:10:40,324
I'll show you! Your heart is mine!

149
00:10:40,524 --> 00:10:42,893
He's still coming onto her?

150
00:10:44,161 --> 00:10:46,763
I'll be back for you, my lady!

151
00:11:00,243 --> 00:11:03,113
Hey, what happened to that Shiratori guy?

152
00:11:03,747 --> 00:11:05,615
Probably still in the hospital.

153
00:11:05,816 --> 00:11:11,722
Man, he's rich like you and Reiko, but he's so different from you guys.

154
00:11:12,055 --> 00:11:15,058
Could be his father in him.

155
00:11:15,258 --> 00:11:16,426
Huh? Do you know him?

156
00:11:17,127 --> 00:11:20,464
Shiratori Ironworks is a subcontractor for my dad's company.

157
00:11:20,664 --> 00:11:22,299
Oh, really?

158
00:11:22,532 --> 00:11:26,603
So he was hitting on you without knowing you were the boss's daughter?

159
00:11:26,803 --> 00:11:28,839
What an idiot!

160
00:11:32,743 --> 00:11:34,311
Speak of the devil...

161
00:11:39,783 --> 00:11:42,285
His driving is still terrible.

162
00:11:49,426 --> 00:11:53,830
Greetings, gutter cops! Great work toiling the streets all day.

163
00:11:54,464 --> 00:11:57,968
Can't hear you! You're too far! Come closer to the police station!

164
00:11:58,335 --> 00:11:59,403
Shut up!

165
00:12:01,872 --> 00:12:04,941
I didn't stall. I stopped there on purpose.

166
00:12:05,142 --> 00:12:07,577
Even the way he walks is creepy.

167
00:12:09,246 --> 00:12:12,716
My lady, I'll have you inside my car today for sure.

168
00:12:13,850 --> 00:12:16,053
She says no. You'll just stall it.

169
00:12:16,286 --> 00:12:17,320
Shut up!

170
00:12:17,521 --> 00:12:20,056
You shouldn't drive what you can't handle.

171
00:12:20,290 --> 00:12:22,325
How dare you!

172
00:12:22,526 --> 00:12:23,360
Hmm?

173
00:12:26,730 --> 00:12:27,864
HANDSOME

174
00:12:28,432 --> 00:12:31,301
You. You're a good looking dude.

175
00:12:31,501 --> 00:12:33,070
The boyfriend, perhaps?

176
00:12:33,303 --> 00:12:34,137
Huh?

177
00:12:34,638 --> 00:12:37,207
If so, you don't stand a chance against me.

178
00:12:37,441 --> 00:12:43,046
For I am rich, good-looking, and educated!

179
00:12:43,280 --> 00:12:46,183
I'm the entire package.

180
00:12:46,383 --> 00:12:47,984
And to top it off...

181
00:12:48,718 --> 00:12:51,221
I've got a pearl white Porsche!

182
00:12:51,621 --> 00:12:52,222
Oh!

183
00:12:54,858 --> 00:12:56,393
You brats!

184
00:12:56,827 --> 00:12:59,229
-Uh-oh! -Run for it!

185
00:13:01,398 --> 00:13:03,733
Damn, they used permanent markers!

186
00:13:03,934 --> 00:13:06,069
This is why I hate the poor side of town!

187
00:13:06,303 --> 00:13:08,038
Hey, a tattooed Porsche!

188
00:13:08,238 --> 00:13:09,840
Shut up, you pleb!

189
00:13:10,040 --> 00:13:11,575
Ouch!

190
00:13:11,775 --> 00:13:15,779
Stay back! Can't you see this stack of bills?

191
00:13:16,012 --> 00:13:17,247
Yes, sir!

192
00:13:18,014 --> 00:13:21,651
Oh no! Seeing money instinctively makes me grovel.

193
00:13:21,852 --> 00:13:23,487
He whacked him with cash?

194
00:13:23,687 --> 00:13:26,756
You don't even know the hardships of inheritance tax...

195
00:13:27,390 --> 00:13:29,259
You! What's your salary?

196
00:13:29,493 --> 00:13:31,561
Um, about 220,000 yen a month...

197
00:13:31,761 --> 00:13:34,664
That is the price for just one custom-made shoe!

198
00:13:34,865 --> 00:13:38,602
What? My salary can only buy one shoe?

199
00:13:38,802 --> 00:13:40,570
I feel so wretched.

200
00:13:40,770 --> 00:13:42,506
You? What's your yearly income?

201
00:13:42,706 --> 00:13:43,940
No idea.

202
00:13:44,341 --> 00:13:45,742
About 7 million yen.

203
00:13:45,942 --> 00:13:49,279
That amount could get you a diamond-encrusted Rolax gold watch!

204
00:13:49,513 --> 00:13:50,680
Yes, sir!

205
00:13:50,881 --> 00:13:52,249
Damn it, I did it again.

206
00:13:52,449 --> 00:13:56,152
Never look down your nose at Super-Rich Reiji Shiratori!

207
00:13:56,386 --> 00:13:59,756
Do you see now how we are in different leagues, you and I?

208
00:14:03,760 --> 00:14:05,362
Yes, you do understand.

209
00:14:06,096 --> 00:14:10,967
Come, my lady. We don't want their poor-people smell rubbing off on us.

210
00:14:11,168 --> 00:14:13,703
Let us go have a fancy meal together.

211
00:14:14,638 --> 00:14:17,908
Would you shut up already?!

212
00:14:20,610 --> 00:14:22,546
Uh-oh, Reiko-san's snapped.

213
00:14:25,181 --> 00:14:26,449
You had your chance!

214
00:14:26,650 --> 00:14:29,586
-Stop it, Reiko! -Let go, Ryo-chan. Let me go!

215
00:14:29,786 --> 00:14:31,187
Calm down, Reiko!

216
00:14:31,421 --> 00:14:33,623
Doesn't it bother you, what he said?

217
00:14:33,823 --> 00:14:36,793
The Ryo-chan I know would have already sent him flying.

218
00:14:36,993 --> 00:14:42,632
This is true, but a man like him could be capable of anything if you hurt his ego.

219
00:14:42,832 --> 00:14:44,401
Just go out for dinner.

220
00:14:44,601 --> 00:14:45,602
What?

221
00:14:45,802 --> 00:14:47,871
Not just you and him, of course.

222
00:14:48,104 --> 00:14:53,009
Our shift will be over soon, so Nakagawa and I will go with you as bodyguards.

223
00:14:53,210 --> 00:14:56,613
Oh? Are you trying to score a free meal?

224
00:14:56,813 --> 00:15:00,317
Well, I'm only going to make sure you're safe...

225
00:15:00,517 --> 00:15:03,620
All right. But only if you're coming.

226
00:15:03,820 --> 00:15:05,789
Okay, that's settled then.

227
00:15:08,425 --> 00:15:13,196
Jeez, why must I treat those bozos as well?

228
00:15:14,064 --> 00:15:15,632
Did you say something?

229
00:15:15,832 --> 00:15:22,539
I was just saying how nice it'll be to let some peasants feel rich for once.

230
00:15:24,207 --> 00:15:25,842
My Ferrari fits four, you know?

231
00:15:26,309 --> 00:15:29,212
Can't bruise his ego by following in a Ferrari.

232
00:15:29,446 --> 00:15:32,048
We need to build him up so he'll treat us well.

233
00:15:32,249 --> 00:15:33,717
And Reiko is our bait.

234
00:15:33,917 --> 00:15:37,320
Wow! Those with limited finances sure come up with great ideas!

235
00:15:38,521 --> 00:15:41,891
But the guy's driving... We'll be here until dawn at this rate.

236
00:15:42,092 --> 00:15:44,260
He won't go above first gear at all.

237
00:15:44,494 --> 00:15:48,498
I see. Reiko Akimoto. That's a nice name.

238
00:15:48,698 --> 00:15:50,567
So, where do you live?

239
00:15:50,800 --> 00:15:51,801
In Hiroo.

240
00:15:52,002 --> 00:15:56,006
Oh, that's the next most upscale residential area after Den-en-chofu.

241
00:15:56,206 --> 00:15:58,208
Do you live with your parents?

242
00:15:58,408 --> 00:16:00,076
No, by myself.

243
00:16:00,276 --> 00:16:03,546
Oh, so it's a one-room apartment?

244
00:16:03,747 --> 00:16:05,815
Actually, it's got four bedrooms.

245
00:16:06,016 --> 00:16:07,851
What? Oh, I see.

246
00:16:08,051 --> 00:16:10,854
The rent must be pretty high then?

247
00:16:11,054 --> 00:16:14,090
My father bought it for me, so I don't pay any rent.

248
00:16:14,291 --> 00:16:18,561
Y-You're pretty rich, aren't you? So, where does your family live?

249
00:16:18,762 --> 00:16:19,696
Ashiya.

250
00:16:19,896 --> 00:16:22,198
That's like the Den-en-chofu of Kansai!

251
00:16:22,399 --> 00:16:26,136
So is it about the same size as mine? Around 150 tsubo?

252
00:16:26,369 --> 00:16:28,104
A little bigger, I think.

253
00:16:28,304 --> 00:16:29,439
200 tsubo?

254
00:16:29,673 --> 00:16:30,540
A bit more.

255
00:16:30,740 --> 00:16:32,275
So, 300 tsubo?

256
00:16:32,509 --> 00:16:34,077
I think it's around 500 tsubo.

257
00:16:34,277 --> 00:16:35,445
500 tsubo!

258
00:16:39,516 --> 00:16:41,451
Idiot. He stalled again.

259
00:16:48,325 --> 00:16:52,796
Don't fret over 500 tsubo, Reiji. It's probably out in the boonies.

260
00:16:53,263 --> 00:16:57,434
By the way, I went to Oukei. What university did you go to?

261
00:16:57,634 --> 00:16:58,802
Sophie University.

262
00:16:59,002 --> 00:17:00,303
She beat me!

263
00:17:01,071 --> 00:17:04,007
That's a great university for debutantes.

264
00:17:04,240 --> 00:17:07,243
Isn't it an escalator school for affiliated kindergartens?

265
00:17:07,444 --> 00:17:09,012
I only went to the university.

266
00:17:09,245 --> 00:17:12,348
Before that was the Lausanne school of Saint Cauria University.

267
00:17:12,749 --> 00:17:13,983
I don't know that one.

268
00:17:14,184 --> 00:17:18,355
It's a very strict boarding school. You've never heard of it?

269
00:17:18,588 --> 00:17:22,092
I've heard of it. It's in Chiba, isn't it?

270
00:17:22,292 --> 00:17:24,160
-It's in Switzerland. -Switzerland!

271
00:17:28,798 --> 00:17:31,134
Shiratori-san, would you like me to drive?

272
00:17:31,334 --> 00:17:32,969
No, I'm fine.

273
00:17:33,169 --> 00:17:36,639
But there's a lot of traffic piling up behind us.

274
00:17:36,840 --> 00:17:39,743
You idiot! Get a move on!

275
00:17:49,652 --> 00:17:51,855
Oh! Reiko took over!

276
00:17:52,055 --> 00:17:54,357
Reiko-san has an advanced driving license.

277
00:17:54,591 --> 00:17:57,293
Please follow closely, and try not to lose her.

278
00:17:57,494 --> 00:17:58,328
Okay.

279
00:18:13,510 --> 00:18:15,245
Wow, she's so good!

280
00:18:23,820 --> 00:18:26,823
I come here often. It's very good.

281
00:18:27,357 --> 00:18:29,325
Oh, it's you, Miss Akimoto.

282
00:18:29,859 --> 00:18:33,062
And Mr. Nakagawa is with you as well?

283
00:18:33,263 --> 00:18:35,265
-Welcome. -Thank you.

284
00:18:35,498 --> 00:18:36,833
Please, follow me.

285
00:18:37,033 --> 00:18:40,036
Hey! Why didn't you greet me?

286
00:18:40,270 --> 00:18:42,806
I'm sorry sir, but who are you?

287
00:18:43,339 --> 00:18:46,576
How rude! I'm Reiji Shiratori. I made this reservation.

288
00:18:46,810 --> 00:18:48,812
And I'm paying as well.

289
00:18:53,283 --> 00:18:54,918
Oh, I do apologize.

290
00:18:55,118 --> 00:19:00,089
Your reservation was for two, but we'll seat you at a table for four.

291
00:19:00,423 --> 00:19:01,591
Please follow me.

292
00:19:02,725 --> 00:19:06,262
I'd have expected as much from Reiko-san,

293
00:19:06,663 --> 00:19:10,900
but you've also been to a five-star restaurant such as this one?

294
00:19:11,401 --> 00:19:13,403
Oh, it's only once or twice.

295
00:19:13,603 --> 00:19:18,374
Oh? Only once or twice? Well, that's not as shocking then.

296
00:19:19,008 --> 00:19:20,577
Once or twice a week.

297
00:19:21,110 --> 00:19:23,246
Hey, super-rich guy! You got this!

298
00:19:26,950 --> 00:19:27,884
SUPER RICH

299
00:19:28,084 --> 00:19:30,019
It's not about the number of times.

300
00:19:30,220 --> 00:19:35,024
What matters is how much money you spend each time.

301
00:19:35,225 --> 00:19:38,294
Go ahead. Order whatever you want.

302
00:19:38,495 --> 00:19:41,498
You super-rich guys are really generous, aren't you?

303
00:19:41,731 --> 00:19:42,632
You think so?

304
00:19:46,569 --> 00:19:50,573
I looked this place up on Tokyo Date Map, but turns out she's a regular here.

305
00:19:51,341 --> 00:19:54,077
May I take your order, sir?

306
00:19:54,410 --> 00:19:56,746
Huh? Oh yes, my order.

307
00:19:56,946 --> 00:19:58,081
Um... Huh?!

308
00:20:01,317 --> 00:20:04,187
I can't read it. It's all in French.

309
00:20:04,420 --> 00:20:06,322
Hey, what's the hold up?

310
00:20:06,523 --> 00:20:11,327
Well, everything here is so delicious. I can't decide.

311
00:20:11,527 --> 00:20:12,462
What should I do?

312
00:20:12,662 --> 00:20:14,664
Screw it. I'll just go down the list!

313
00:20:14,898 --> 00:20:18,001
I think I'll have number 20, the chef's special course.

314
00:20:18,201 --> 00:20:21,137
Huh? Oh, what a coincidence.

315
00:20:21,337 --> 00:20:24,007
I was just about to order that too.

316
00:20:24,207 --> 00:20:27,377
The mega rich really do think alike.

317
00:20:30,146 --> 00:20:31,147
I'll have that too.

318
00:20:31,347 --> 00:20:32,282
Me too.

319
00:20:32,482 --> 00:20:33,917
Very good.

320
00:20:35,385 --> 00:20:38,521
Hmm? Miss Akimoto and Mr. Nakagawa?

321
00:20:39,656 --> 00:20:42,458
What a pleasure to see the both of you. Welcome.

322
00:20:42,659 --> 00:20:45,361
If you'd like, the VIP room is available.

323
00:20:45,562 --> 00:20:51,301
Oh, you recognized me as vice president of Shiratori Ironworks? Let's move then.

324
00:20:51,501 --> 00:20:52,502
Huh?

325
00:20:53,703 --> 00:20:55,171
We'll be fine here.

326
00:20:55,371 --> 00:20:56,973
Understood.

327
00:20:58,508 --> 00:21:00,143
Hey, stop! Wait!

328
00:21:00,343 --> 00:21:03,046
I said we'd move, damn it!

329
00:21:03,246 --> 00:21:06,883
It's okay. You're a Mr. Moneybags. Water under the bridge for you!

330
00:21:10,353 --> 00:21:11,220
MR. MONEYBAGS

331
00:21:11,654 --> 00:21:14,557
I have always wanted to try commoner dining, after all.

332
00:21:14,791 --> 00:21:16,693
Can I order steak too?

333
00:21:16,893 --> 00:21:18,061
Go ahead.

334
00:21:18,261 --> 00:21:20,196
Waiter, add one steak!

335
00:21:20,396 --> 00:21:21,998
Jeez, Ryo-chan.

336
00:21:22,198 --> 00:21:22,832
Hmm?

337
00:21:23,032 --> 00:21:27,704
If you're going with the special course, I recommend the 1982 Bordeaux.

338
00:21:27,904 --> 00:21:31,040
Perhaps the 1983 would be better than the 1982?

339
00:21:31,240 --> 00:21:34,043
You really know your wine, Mr. Nakagawa.

340
00:21:34,243 --> 00:21:35,244
Hey!

341
00:21:35,445 --> 00:21:38,514
I'm the one with the money paying for all this, you know!

342
00:21:38,715 --> 00:21:40,083
You should ask me first!

343
00:21:40,283 --> 00:21:41,150
Huh?

344
00:21:41,351 --> 00:21:44,354
What reason could you have for asking him over me?

345
00:21:44,554 --> 00:21:48,224
Why is everyone here ignoring me?

346
00:21:48,424 --> 00:21:49,459
Hey, Reiji!

347
00:21:49,692 --> 00:21:51,728
Oh, Dad...

348
00:21:52,061 --> 00:21:54,097
My, is that your son?

349
00:21:54,297 --> 00:21:56,733
Yeah. Give me a minute.

350
00:21:57,300 --> 00:21:58,601
Fancy seeing you here.

351
00:21:58,935 --> 00:22:01,371
I see you're having a good time, Dad.

352
00:22:01,571 --> 00:22:03,773
Don't tell your mom, okay?

353
00:22:04,007 --> 00:22:04,774
Hmm?

354
00:22:06,275 --> 00:22:10,079
Hey, that's a nice lass you got there. Which bar did you fish her from?

355
00:22:10,279 --> 00:22:15,418
Stop it, you. I don't go around picking up girls in bars like you, Dad.

356
00:22:15,618 --> 00:22:18,488
But that doesn't mean I won't get her in the sack.

357
00:22:20,456 --> 00:22:21,891
Introductions. This is...

358
00:22:24,394 --> 00:22:25,795
Hello, Mr. Shiratori.

359
00:22:28,431 --> 00:22:30,066
Huh? You know her?

360
00:22:30,266 --> 00:22:32,068
You idiot!

361
00:22:32,602 --> 00:22:37,774
She's the daughter of Akimoto Trading! She's way out of your league!

362
00:22:38,274 --> 00:22:42,278
Miss Akimoto, my profuse apologies for my son's idiotic and rude behavior.

363
00:22:42,745 --> 00:22:45,748
Oh, there's no need to apologize.

364
00:22:46,249 --> 00:22:50,953
Absolutely there is! We are forever in Akimoto Trading's debt.

365
00:22:51,154 --> 00:22:52,822
D-Dad!

366
00:22:53,056 --> 00:22:56,325
He didn't know it was you. Please forgive his ignorance!

367
00:22:56,526 --> 00:22:58,294
I'm not really...

368
00:22:58,494 --> 00:23:00,897
All that money isn't helping now, huh?

369
00:23:01,097 --> 00:23:01,964
Nope.

370
00:23:02,765 --> 00:23:05,501
Haven't seen Shiratori since. Wonder how he's doing?

371
00:23:05,702 --> 00:23:07,470
I feel a little bad for him.

372
00:23:08,071 --> 00:23:09,939
None of it was your fault though.

373
00:23:10,139 --> 00:23:13,176
-He was the one who asked you out. -But still...

374
00:23:13,976 --> 00:23:14,944
Greetings!

375
00:23:15,144 --> 00:23:16,312
It's you!

376
00:23:16,979 --> 00:23:18,815
Shiratori-san?

377
00:23:19,015 --> 00:23:21,384
Why do you look like that?

378
00:23:22,652 --> 00:23:27,256
My father disowned me that night. Now I'm super poor, like you.

379
00:23:27,557 --> 00:23:28,925
I'm really sorry.

380
00:23:29,125 --> 00:23:31,828
Tut, tut. Don't worry about it.

381
00:23:32,028 --> 00:23:36,466
I'll climb my way back up and become even more mega rich.

382
00:23:36,666 --> 00:23:38,034
Until then, farewell!

383
00:23:41,838 --> 00:23:42,972
He never learns.

384
00:23:43,172 --> 00:23:46,542
Hurry up and make that big money so you can treat us again!

385
00:23:49,011 --> 00:23:50,813
Yeah! Mr. Moneybags!

386
00:24:02,959 --> 00:24:08,798
RYO-SAN'S GREAT ESCAPE!
